#{[17592186395192 #edb/ref 1080 "images/6a/6aeb70c5041be20ab9c38724e3cf1e1852f491478c32037222beb83372ab7776.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395192 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395192 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "05aad34f-e824-58fd-8635-d142c9e7b023" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395193 #edb/ref 1080 "images/ae/ae362c4e6d675c8d7ca65f2aa3702d65c63b0ffb6e370a573da00532e567ab1c.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395193 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395193 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "020c5584-4a73-53a6-9b88-b65945011b03" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395194 #edb/ref 1080 "images/84/8478a27a046a1e4f7d26534b34f7b4c002ff5cb86bd553937b01ebab8ad61d4f.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395194 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395194 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "42e91f65-6f16-5cdf-9580-e20d5c21cad8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404752 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186404753 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404752 #edb/ref 1069 "q-94997" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404752 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404752 #edb/ref 1071 "Which curve is defined by the equation $5{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+5{x}_{2}^{2}=12?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404752 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "524143ac-0f98-5858-ae7f-d1be1f96a542" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404752 #edb/ref 1074 "Consider the quadratic form $Q(x)=5{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+5{x}_{2}^{2}.$ To determine the curve defined by the given equation, we reduce $Q(x)$ to its canonical (diagonal) form.\n\nFirst, we write down the matrix of $Q(x),$ which is\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNext, we find the eigenvalues of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}5-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 1 & 5-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-10\\lambda +24 & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =6,\\,4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our quadratic form can be reduced to $6{y}_{1}^{2}+4{y}_{2}^{2}.$ \n\nIn the new variables, the curve has the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{y}_{1}^{2}+4{y}_{2}^{2} & =12 \\\\ \\frac{{y}_{1}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}_{2}^{2}}{3} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{y}_{1}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{2})^{2}}+\\frac{{y}_{2}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is an ellipse with semiaxes $\\sqrt{2}$ and $\\sqrt{3}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186404753 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404754 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404753 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404755 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404753 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404756 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404753 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404757 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404753 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404758 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404753 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404753 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404753 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186404754 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404753 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "23ec9caf-4548-5197-b9d1-b78a71376df8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404754 #edb/ref 1080 "An ellipse with semiaxes $\\sqrt{2}$ and $\\sqrt{3}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404754 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404754 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ffef5c19-fd74-5ba0-af4d-7b043c0b9bc6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404755 #edb/ref 1080 "An ellipse with semiaxes $1$ and $\\sqrt{2}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404755 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404755 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f3838d79-b19d-50cb-bda4-8a032786b6e6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404756 #edb/ref 1080 "A circle of radius $2$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404756 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404756 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c768ce44-3d75-5d9d-b7e6-297ae3bec501" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404757 #edb/ref 1080 "A hyperbola with semiaxes $3$ and $\\sqrt{2}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404757 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404757 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0ddd23b0-eb68-5321-80ed-2e347cdf3572" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404758 #edb/ref 1080 "A hyperbola with semiaxes $\\sqrt{3}$ and $2$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404758 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404758 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "bff4817a-3051-5961-a312-060e27c50a46" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405181 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186405182 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405181 #edb/ref 1069 "q-97995" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405181 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405181 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$ and the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,Ax.$ Given that $A$ has eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}=0$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-4,$ find unit vectors along the principal axes of the quadratic form." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186405181 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "091c06c4-0cfd-5952-9df6-eba9b260f93a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405181 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that $A$ is symmetric. \nThe principal axes of the quadratic form \n\n$$\n{x}^{T}\\,Ax\n$$\n\nare the vectors that give an orthonormal eigenvector basis for $A.$ Let's now find these eigenvectors.\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-0I & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}-0\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(A-0I)x=0$ gives the eigenvector ${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$ Dividing ${v}_{1}$ by its norm $‖{v}_{1}‖=\\sqrt{2},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{{v}_{1}}{‖{v}_{1}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=-4,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-(-4)I & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}+4\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(A+4I)x=0$ gives the eigenvector ${v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$ Dividing ${v}_{2}$ by its norm $‖{v}_{2}‖=\\sqrt{2},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{{v}_{2}}{‖{v}_{2}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, unit vectors along the principal axes of our quadratic form are\n\n$\\,$ $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186405182 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186405183 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405182 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186405184 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405182 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186405185 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405182 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186405186 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405182 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186405187 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405182 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405182 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405182 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186405184 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405182 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "efb02de0-491f-59d6-8a75-57bfea7150b9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405183 #edb/ref 1080 "$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186405183 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405183 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e022e2a9-7ada-59ab-9b55-0e78c7221355" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405184 #edb/ref 1080 "$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186405184 #edb/ref 1082 #